# The Daily Lens

A responsive News / Blog Portal student project made with plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Class serial number 11 maps to Practical 12.

## Run locally

1. Open this folder in VS Code.
2. Open `index.html` in a browser, or use the Live Server extension for a smoother development experience.
3. Use the navigation to visit all seven pages: Home, Categories, Trending, Article, Write a Post, About, and Contact.

No build tools or package installation are required. Internet is needed for the Google Fonts and Unsplash demo images. If an image URL is unavailable, replace it with a local image.

## Features

- Responsive desktop, tablet, and mobile layout
- Story category tabs and instant search (press `/` to focus search, `Esc` to clear)
- Like and bookmark controls stored in browser local storage
- Reader posts saved in local storage and shown in story listings
- Trending list sorted by likes
- Light / dark mode saved in local storage
- Share action using the Web Share API where available, clipboard otherwise
- Reading-time estimates, newsletter sign-up demo, and contact form validation
- Mobile navigation and back-to-top button

## Storage and demo limitations

This is a static front-end project. Posts, likes, bookmarks, theme preference, and newsletter demo sign-ups are stored only in the current browser. The contact form shows a confirmation but does not send email. There is no server, user account, or cross-device publishing.

## Project files

- `index.html` — Home page
- `categories.html` — Category directory and filtered stories
- `trending.html` — Most-liked stories
- `article.html` — Article detail and share controls
- `write.html` — Reader post form
- `about.html` — Project mission and team
- `contact.html` — Contact form
- `styles.css` — Shared responsive styling
- `app.js` — Story content and interactions
